latticelink3dnl_rotation.out
LatticeLink3dNL large-rotation kinematic check. Matrix node 1 rotated about y to pi/2 (rebar node 2 clamped). Rigid arm (0,0,-0.011) swings with the matrix rotation, so the axial slip = 0.011*sin(theta_y). This verifies the corotational rigid-arm route: a linear link would give 0.011*theta_y (0.01728 at pi/2). The check reads the strain (slip), so it is a pure kinematic test, independent of the bond material response.
NonLinearStatic nmsteps 1 nsteps 6 contextOutputStep 1000 nmodules 1
nsteps 6 rtolf 1.e-3 maxiter 300 stiffMode 1 controllmode 1 refloadmode 1 minsteplength 1.e-3
errorcheck
domain 3dLattice
OutputManager tstep_all dofman_all element_all
ndofman 2 nelem 1 ncrosssect 1 nmat 1 nbc 2 nic 0 nltf 2
node 1 coords 3 0.0 0.0  0.000 bc 6 1 1 1 1 2 1
node 2 coords 3 0.0 0.0 -0.011 bc 6 1 1 1 0 1 1
latticelink3Dnl 1 nodes 2 1 2 crossSect 1 mat 1 length 2.5e-2 diameter 5.2e-3 dirvector 3 1.0 0.0 0.0
LatticeCS 1 material 1 shape 1 radius 0.0026
LatticeSlip 1 d 1. talpha 0.0 e 200.e9 a1 100. a2 100. t0 4.e6 type 1 s1 1.e-5 alpha 0.5
BoundaryCondition 1 loadTimeFunction 1 prescribedvalue 0.0
BoundaryCondition 2 loadTimeFunction 2 prescribedvalue 1.5707963
ConstantFunction 1 f(t) 1.0
PiecewiseLinFunction 2 nPoints 2 t 2 0. 6. f(t) 2 0. 1.
#%BEGIN_CHECK% tolerance 1.e-4
## Axial slip (latticestrain comp 1) = 0.011*sin(theta_y), theta_y = (t/6)*pi/2.
## tStep 3: theta=pi/4 -> 0.011*sin(pi/4) = 7.7782e-3  (a linear link would give 8.6394e-3)
## tStep 6: theta=pi/2 -> 0.011*sin(pi/2) = 1.1000e-2  (a linear link would give 1.7279e-2)
## keyword 138 = IST_LatticeStrain (numeric code); component 1 = axial slip.
#ELEMENT tStep 3 number 1 gp 1 keyword 138 component 1 value 7.7782e-3
#ELEMENT tStep 6 number 1 gp 1 keyword 138 component 1 value 1.1000e-2
#%END_CHECK%
